# Code owners for the Musher catalog.
#
# A catch-all is deliberate here: this repository is a single curated content
# corpus with one owning team, so every path wants the same reviewer. (The
# platform monorepo bans a catch-all because its review gate is paired with a
# branch ruleset that turns one into blanket review — that pairing does not
# exist here.)
#
# This file and the CI configuration (.github/) keep an owner of their own, so
# a change to who reviews, or to how CI checks the catalog, goes through that
# owner. The last matching pattern wins, so they follow the catch-all.
#
# GitHub silently ignores an owner without write access, so verify access when
# adding one.

